<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default">
<!--
    Kuna #63 (personal): P1 relocatable-object layout, instruction relocation
    families (option relocobjects, default on). Objects built from
    fixtures/relocs/t.c and a64.s as their headers say. Before this change
    each family below was "unsupported" and its field kept the assembler's
    placeholder: RISC-V HI20/LO12 data read as address 0 and the tail call a
    switch, MIPS HI16/LO16 data read as dat_0 and the jal as sub_0, PPC32
    ADDR16_HA/LO data read as dat_0.
    mipspic.o is PIC: before, every $gp load stayed *(t9 + off) and the call
    went through an unknown pointer, because a big-endian object got no
    rebased analyzer view (so no t9 = entry seed) and GOT16/CALL16 were
    unsupported.
    #1-#2 AArch64 ADR_PREL_LO21, LD_PREL_LO19, MOVW_UABS_G1/G0_NC,
    CONDBR19, TSTBR14. #3 RISC-V HI20/LO12_I/LO12_S. #10 RISC-V CALL (tail) to an extern: its
    one destination has no bytes, so tailcalljump takes it as a tail call. #4-#5 MIPS REL HI16/LO16
    pairing and R_MIPS_26 (#5 also covers CALL16 in mipspic.o). #8-#9 MIPS
    _gp_disp, local GOT16+LO16 page entries, global GOT16. #6-#7 PPC32 ADDR16_HA/LO and REL24.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">c3</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
